{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1438","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Powerful Ksenia"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ksenia has an array $$$a$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ positive integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In one operation she can do the following: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" choose three distinct indices $$$i$$$, $$$j$$$, $$$k$$$, and then "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" change all of $$$a_i, a_j, a_k$$$ to $$$a_i \\oplus a_j \\oplus a_k$$$ simultaneously, where $$$\\oplus$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#XOR"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise XOR operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"She wants to make all $$$a_i$$$ equal "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"in at most $$$n$$$ operations"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", or to determine that it is impossible to do so. She wouldn't ask for your help, but please, help her!"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\leq n \\leq 10^5$$$) — the length of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers, $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_i \\leq 10^9$$$) — elements of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the first line depending on whether it is possible to make all elements equal in at most $$$n$$$ operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is possible, print an integer $$$m$$$ ($$$0 \\leq m \\leq n$$$), which denotes the number of operations you do."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In each of the next $$$m$$$ lines, print three distinct integers $$$i, j, k$$$, representing one operation. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are many such operation sequences possible, print any. Note that you do "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" have to minimize the number of operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n4 2 1 7 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\n1\n1 3 4"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n10 4 49 22\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, the array becomes $$$[4 \\oplus 1 \\oplus 7, 2, 4 \\oplus 1 \\oplus 7, 4 \\oplus 1 \\oplus 7, 2] = [2, 2, 2, 2, 2]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1438D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1438/problem/D"}